Author: CusDeb OS Team
Description: Export OpenThemeDataForDpi from uxtheme (non-Vista spec).
 Wine 11 comctl32 calls OpenThemeDataForDpi for themed controls
 (listview, toolbar, treeview). The delay-load resolves against the
 loaded uxtheme.dll, which is our ReactOS one; without this export the
 lookup fails, an exception is raised inside the control's window proc,
 and themed painting aborts mid-way, leaving blank white icons on the
 desktop, the taskbar and explorer list views. The implementation in
 system.c already exists, it just was not exported in uxtheme.spec.
Last-Modified: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 17:45:00 +0300

--- a/src/dll/win32/uxtheme/uxtheme.spec
+++ b/src/dll/win32/uxtheme/uxtheme.spec
@@ -93,3 +93,4 @@
 93 stdcall SetThemeAppProperties(long)
 94 stdcall SetWindowTheme(ptr wstr wstr)
 95 stdcall ThemeInitApiHook(long ptr)
+@ stdcall OpenThemeDataForDpi(ptr wstr long)
